LAY-005 (dummy chains for long-span edges) landed as commit `cc38406` on branch `docs/ai-agent-guide` and pushed. 8 files changed, 21 new tests, `pnpm run gates` green (typecheck+lint+verify+test; 1537 passed / 6 skipped). Dummies drive ordering via barycenter; their collapsed positions become router bend hints stored on `StructuralEdgeGeometry.intermediate`. One deliberate deferral: dummies are excluded from BK compaction (positions interpolated from placed real endpoints) because full BK participation reproducibly inflated prune-wall enough to break perimeter routing — full participation is a natural follow-up when the channel router (PRF-003) lands. `chooseDummyParent` helper shipped with 4-case tests; wire-up trivial when nested top-level containers exist in the model.
